<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 3.51 percent.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index down 3.51 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index fell 2.56 points, 3.51 percent, to 70.42 points after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index fell 50.09 points to 3,256.96.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over the local market was 7.46 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove Index is a capitalisation weighted basket Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
</text>
